Measured, OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 ./.venv/bin/python, 240 rows, group base rates split by s=="a", base_estimator=DummyClassifier(strategy="most_frequent"), a.compare_methods(...):
  Reductions   acc=0.6916666666666667 viol=0.0 satisfied=True params={method: reductions, constraint_evaluated: True}
  Threshold    acc=0.6916666666666667 viol=0.0 satisfied=True params={method: threshold, constraint_evaluated: True}
  Grid_Search  acc=0.6916666666666667 viol=0.0 satisfied=True params={method: grid_search, constraint_evaluated: True}
  warnings during the whole call: 1, and it is raised INSIDE ExponentiatedGradient, for the reductions arm only.
All three accuracies are byte-identical to the majority-class rate, i.e. all three "mitigations" collapsed to a constant classifier and are trivially perfectly fair because they made no decision. Threshold and grid_search produced NO warning at all. The flag that records this exists upstream: ExponentiatedGradient.fit writes fairness_metrics["degenerate_constant_predictions"] and FairClassifierResult carries fairness_metrics, and this method builds MethodComparison with parameters = {"method": ..., "constraint_evaluated": ...} only, so the flag is dropped at the boundary and no consumer of the returned list, no recommendation and no report can see it. The result: a.generate_recommendation(cmp) then returned "Reductions" at priority HIGH with the rationale "Achieves fairness constraint with best accuracy (0.692)", 0 warnings.
Second gap on the same boundary: FairClassifier computes accuracy as float(np.mean(y_pred == y)) at sklearn_wrappers.py:273/328/366/571 with no unscorable-row guard, and this method passes it straight into MethodComparison with no accuracy_measured key, while its SIBLING arm evaluate_baseline (row 9 of this batch) was given exactly that three-state treatment. Both arms feed the same MethodComparison objects into the same report and the same renderers.
Attack 4: the graded partial-failure disclosure itself is present

vfairness.in_processing.analyzer.baselin.audit_evidence:
Measured, OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 ./.venv/bin/python, 40 rows, sensitive_by_attr={"sex": 20 f then 20 m}, y_pred_baseline and y_pred_fair both real 0/1 arrays, before/after metrics carrying demographic_parity_difference 0.30 and 0.05:
